# Run it yourself

When a task can be done in this environment (train, plot, regenerate figures, run scripts), **do it** — do not tell the user how to repeat it.

## Do

- Run commands and report outcomes (paths to outputs, brief results).
- Link to generated artifacts with workspace-relative paths.
- Ask before long or destructive runs only when scope or cost is unclear.

## Don't

- End responses with copy-paste commands for reruns the user did not ask for.
- Say "you can run …" or "to regenerate, run …" unless they explicitly want the command for their own terminal.

If something failed or was skipped, fix or run it — don't hand off instructions.
